; A process with more than half its 64 MB cap live collects before it
; reaches the cap (D196), rather than failing there with a heap of
; garbage: 2.4 million cells (38 MB) kept, then 3,000 lists of a thousand
; cells (48 MB) made and dropped. Collecting at twice what's live, its
; next collection would have been past the cap.

(defun garbage (n acc)
    (if (== n 0) acc (garbage (- n 1) (+ acc (length (range 0 1000))))))

(let keep (range 0 2400000))
(pprint (garbage 3000 0))
(pprint (length keep))
:done
